---
description: Desktop (Electron) app must use backend base URL for all API calls
globs: desktop/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Desktop API Calls

The desktop app runs in Electron. Relative URLs like `fetch('/api/...')` resolve to the Electron app origin, NOT the Python backend. This returns HTML and causes JSON parse errors.

Always use the backend base URL for API calls:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hits Electron origin, returns HTML
const res = await fetch('/api/analytics')

// ✅ GOOD — hits the Python backend
const [baseUrl, setBaseUrl] = useState('http://127.0.0.1:8000')

useEffect(() => {
  if (window.electronAPI?.getBackendUrl) {
    window.electronAPI.getBackendUrl().then(setBaseUrl)
  }
}, [])

const res = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/api/analytics`)
```

For pages with many API calls, use the existing `ApiService` from `desktop/src/services/api.ts` which handles this automatically.

The frontend app (non-Electron) uses Vite proxy so relative URLs work there — this rule is desktop-only.
